<!--
  Slide 11 — Governance Metrics (10, 12)
  Type: content-slide
  Required tokens (substituted by render_deck.py from metrics.json):
    {{M10_MULT}}, {{M10_CONF}}, {{M10_CONF_LABEL}}, {{M10_CAVEAT}}  Approved Exceptions
    {{M12_MULT}}, {{M12_CONF}}, {{M12_CONF_LABEL}}, {{M12_CAVEAT}}  Defects Out of SLA
  Required non-text visual: <table> + Lucide icons

  Authority: AAP §0.4.1 (file inventory enumerates this filename), §0.2.3
  (no admin token → Metric 10 Low confidence; no SLA source → Metric 12
  Insufficient signal), §0.7.1 Rule 5 (content-slide constraints — max
  4 bullets, ≤40 body words, ≥1 non-text visual, zero emoji), §0.7.2.1
  ("MUST NOT fabricate, estimate, or extrapolate. Report 'Insufficient
  signal — [reason]' when data is lacking."), §0.7.2.2 Rule 3
  (Confidence Transparency — Low metrics MUST carry a caveat).

  Rendering notes:
    - This template is consumed by render_deck.py, which substitutes the
      eight tokens above from metrics.json and writes the result into
      acceleration/executive-presentation.html.
    - The MULT cell holds either a numeric multiplier (e.g., "1.0x")
      OR the literal phrase "Insufficient signal — <reason>". The phrasing
      "Insufficient signal" is canonical per AAP §0.7.2.1 and MUST NOT be
      replaced by editorial framing such as "unavailable" or "missing".
    - The CONF token expands to the CSS class suffix
      ("high" | "medium" | "low"), so the rendered span becomes
      <span class="confidence-low">Low</span>. The badge styles are
      defined in acceleration/templates/deck/theme.css
      (.confidence-high / .confidence-medium / .confidence-low).
    - Lucide icons: shield-alert (governance/exception warning, Metric 10)
      and clock-alert (SLA/time warning, Metric 12). Both icon names are
      available in Lucide 0.460.0, the version pinned by AAP §0.6.1.
    - The renderer is the single source of truth for these values; the
      same numbers MUST appear in acceleration-report.md, the Traceability
      Matrix, and the Acceleration Curve table, satisfying Rule 4
      (Internal Consistency).
-->
<section class="content-slide">
  <span class="eyebrow">Governance</span>
  <h3>Exceptions &amp; SLA (10, 12)</h3>
  <table class="metric-table">
    <colgroup>
      <col class="col-icon">
      <col class="col-metric">
      <col class="col-value">
      <col class="col-conf">
      <col class="col-caveat">
    </colgroup>
    <thead>
      <tr><th></th><th>Metric</th><th>Result</th><th>Confidence</th><th>Caveat</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><i data-lucide="shield-alert" aria-hidden="true"></i></td>
        <td>10 · Approved Exceptions</td>
        <td>{{M10_SHORT}}</td>
        <td><span class="confidence-{{M10_CONF}}">{{M10_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td>
        <td>{{M10_CAVEAT}}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><i data-lucide="clock-alert" aria-hidden="true"></i></td>
        <td>12 · Defects Out of SLA</td>
        <td>{{M12_SHORT}}</td>
        <td><span class="confidence-{{M12_CONF}}">{{M12_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td>
        <td>{{M12_CAVEAT}}</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>
